--- make
description: A route, added to routes.kscript (or api.kscript with --api), with its controller made if it's missing
category: Routes and APIs
usage: <path> [--method get|post|put|patch|delete] [--api] [--to controller.action] [--resource] [--view name] [--name route.name]
--method: The HTTP method: get (the default), post, put, patch, delete, options or any
--api: Add it to api.kscript, served under /api with JSON errors, instead of routes.kscript
--to: The controller function that answers it, such as people.list. By default the path picks it: users gives users.index, users/{id} gives users.show, and --method post gives users.store
--controller: The controller to use or make, such as admin/users (default: the path without its {parameters})
--action: The controller function (default from the method: index or show, store, update, destroy)
--resource: Add Resource(path: …, to: …) for index, show, store, update and destroy, and make a resource controller
--view: Answer with this view (made in views/ if it's missing) instead of a controller
--name: A name for @route('name')
--where: Rules for the parameters, such as "id: int"
example: kscript make route users
example: kscript make route "users/{id}" --where "id: int"
example: kscript make route users --method post --api
example: kscript make route people --resource --api
example: kscript make route about --view about
example: kscript make route reports/export --to reports.export
adds-to: routes
---
{{#if resource}}
Resource(path: "{{ route_path }}", to: {{ alias }})
{{else}}
{{#if view}}
Get(path: "{{ route_path }}", view: "{{ view }}"{{#if route_name}}, name: "{{ route_name }}"{{/if}})
{{else}}
{{ method }}(path: "{{ route_path }}", to: @{{ alias }}.{{ action }}{{#if route_name}}, name: "{{ route_name }}"{{/if}}{{#if where}}, where: "{{ where }}"{{/if}})
{{/if}}
{{/if}}
